.TH AVR\-TOKEN\-REVOKE 1 "" "avr 0.4.1" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-token-revoke \- Revoke a token.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr token revoke
[OPTIONS] TOKEN_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Revoke a token.
.PP
Requests made with the token are refused from then on. Revoking a token that is already revoked succeeds.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr token revoke key-abc123
    avr token revoke key-abc123 --yes
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fITOKEN_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR, \fB\-y\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-token (1),
.BR avr-token-create (1),
.BR avr-token-list (1),
.BR avr-token-view (1)
